# AI Trophy Scoring Feature Plan

## Overview
Add AI-powered Boone & Crockett score estimation for deer, using user-cropped head/antler photos analyzed by Gemini's top model. This is a premium add-on feature.

## Research Summary

### B&C Scoring System
The Boone & Crockett scoring system measures:
- **F** - Main beam length (both sides)
- **G** - Tine/point lengths (G1-G7 per side)
- **H** - Circumferences (4 per side, between tines)
- **D** - Inside spread (widest point between beams)

**Gross Score** = Sum of all measurements
**Net Score** = Gross - asymmetry deductions (differences between left/right)

### Reference Measurements (from B&C Field Judging Guide)
These are average buck proportions used for visual estimation:
| Feature | Average Size |
|---------|--------------|
| Ear tip-to-tip spread | 16 inches |
| Ear length (base to tip) | 6 inches |
| Eye circumference | 4 inches |
| Eye to nose | 8 inches |

### MSU Deer Lab Score Estimation Formulas
```
Most Accurate (all 4 measurements):
Score = -34.064 + (4.64 × points) + (0.804 × spread) + (3.075 × circumferences) + (1.942 × main_beams)

Simpler (beams + points + circumferences):
Score = -30.117 + (4.583 × points) + (3.14 × circumferences) + (2.162 × main_beams)
```

### BuckScore Approach (competitor)
- Uses ear width as primary reference measurement
- Requires manual point placement on measurements
- Claims 3% accuracy with proper reference placement
- Best angles: 0°, 45°, 90° (side/quartering views)

